REGENT OF BANTUL

REGENT OF BANTUL

REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANTUL REGENCY

NUMBER 15 OF 2013

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF CHILD AND WOMAN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF BANTUL,

Considering : a. that every child and woman has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain a sense of security, free from all forms of violence, discrimination and violations of the rights of women and children;

b. that acts of violence against children and women continue to increase, thus requiring comprehensive and maximum protection efforts, concrete action, formal institutional support, regulations that can guarantee implementation from the Regional Government in increasing broad public participation;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Child and

Woman Victims of Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 15 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas Within

the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette

of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 44);

3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette

of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic

of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement

to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);

5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

6. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 12 of 2008 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);

7. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);

8. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);

9. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);

10. Government Regulation Number 32 of 1950 concerning Stipulation of the Commencement of Law of 1950 Number 12, 13, 14 and 15 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 59);

11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation of Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);

12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Implementation of Protection of Women;

13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 Concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;

14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Child Victims of Violence;

15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated

Service Centers;

16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence;

17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;

18. Regional Regulation of the Special Region of Yogyakarta Province Number 3 of 2012 concerning Protection of Child and Woman Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of

the Special Region of Yogyakarta Province of 2012

Number 3, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of the Special Region of

Yogyakarta Province Number 3);

19.Regional Regulation of Bantul Regency Number 7 of 2005 concerning Transparency and Public Participation in the Administration of Government in Bantul

Regency (Regional Gazette of Bantul Regency of

2005 Series C Number 1);

20.Regional Regulation of Bantul Regency Number 13 of 2007 concerning Stipulation of Mandatory and Optional Government Affairs of Bantul Regency (Regional Gazette of

Bantul Regency of 2007 Series D Number 11);

With Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BANTUL REGENCY, and

THE REGENT OF BANTUL,

HAS DECIDED:

To Stipulate : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF CHILD AND WOMAN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

text:
Pasal 3

(1) Tujuan perlindungan Anak dan Perempuan dari tindak kekerasan adalah : a. mencegah dan menghapus segala bentuk tindak kekerasan dan eksploitasi terhadap anak dan perempuan yang terjadi di lingkungan keluarga maupun masyarakat;

b. mengupayakan pemulihan dan reintegrasi sosial terhadap anak dan perempuan korban tindak kekerasan;

c. memberikan pelayanan kepada anak dan perempuan korban tindak kekerasan, pelapor, dan saksi;

d. melakukan pemberdayaan kepada perempuan korban kekerasan; dan e. meningkatkan partisipasi masyarakat.

(2) Penyelenggaraan perlindungan anak dan perempuan dari tindak kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), meliputi aspek:

a. pencegahan;
b. pelayanan dan pendampingan;
c. reintegrasi sosial; dan
d. pemberdayaan.

translated_text:
Article 3

(1) The objectives of protecting Children and Women from acts of violence are: a. to prevent and eliminate all forms of acts of violence and exploitation against children and women that occur in the family and community environment;

b. to seek recovery and social reintegration for children and women victims of acts of violence;

c. to provide services to children and women victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses;

d. to empower women victims of violence; and e. to increase community participation.

(2) The organization of protection for children and women from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), includes aspects of:

a. prevention;
b. services and assistance;
c. social reintegration; and
d. empowerment.

text:
Pasal 4

Setiap korban tindak kekerasan mendapatkan hak-hak sebagai berikut: a. hak untuk dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia; b. hak atas pemulihan kesehatan dan psikologis dari penderitaan yang dialami korban;

c. hak menentukan sendiri keputusannya;

d. hak mendapatkan informasi;

e. hak atas kerahasiaan identitasnya;

f. hak pelayanan optimal;

g. hak atas kompensasi;

h. hak penanganan berkelanjutan sampai tahap rehabilitasi sosial; i. hak atas penanganan pengaduan;

j. hak untuk mendapatkan kemudahan dalam proses peradilan; k. hak atas pendampingan psikologis dan hukum; dan

l. hak atas perlindungan dan pelayanan hukum.

translated_text:
Article 4

Every victim of acts of violence receives the following rights: a. the right to have their dignity and honor as a human being respected; b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;

c. the right to make their own decisions;

d. the right to obtain information;

e. the right to confidentiality of their identity;

f. the right to optimal services;

g. the right to compensation;

h. the right to continuous treatment up to the social rehabilitation stage; i. the right to complaint handling;

j. the right to receive facilitation in the judicial process; k. the right to psychological and legal assistance; and

l. the right to legal protection and services.

text:
Pasal 5

Anak korban kekerasan selain mendapatkan hak-hak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 4, juga mendapatkan hak-hak sebagai berikut:

a. hak penghormatan atas kelangsungan hidup, tumbuh dan berkembang; b. hak pelayanan dasar dalam bidang pendidikan;
c. hak pelayanan dasar dalam bidang kesehatan;
d. hak perlindungan yang sama;
e. hak bebas dari berbagai stigma; dan
f. hak mendapatkan kebebasan.

translated_text:
Article 5

Child victims of violence, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 4, also receive the following rights:

a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development; b. the right to basic services in the field of education;
c. the right to basic services in the field of health;
d. the right to equal protection;
e. the right to be free from various stigmas; and
f. the right to obtain freedom.

text:
Pasal 6

Kewajiban dan tanggungjawab dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap anak dan perempuan korban kekerasan adalah:

a. Pemerintah Daerah;
b. masyarakat;
c. keluarga; dan
d. orangtua.

translated_text:
Article 6

The obligations and responsibilities in organizing protection for children and women victims of violence are:

a. Regional Government;
b. community;
c. family; and
d. parents.

text:
Pasal 7

(1) Untuk melaksanakan ketentuan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 6 huruf a, Pemerintah Daerah melaksanakan upaya perlindungan korban, dalam bentuk:

a. merumuskan kebijakan tentang perlindungan Anak dan Perempuan dari segala bentuk tindak kekerasan dan diskriminasi;
b. menyusun perencanaan program dan kegiatan;
c. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana;
d. mengalokasikan anggaran khusus yang responsif gender; e. membentuk PPT dan/atau Rumah Aman;
f. membentuk dan memfasilitasi FPKK; dan
g. melakukan monitoring dan evaluasi.
(2) Dalam hal pelaksanaan kewajiban Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Pemerintah Daerah menyusun Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagai dasar bagi SKPD dalam melaksanakan perlindungan terhadap korban.
(3) Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2), merupakan bagian Rencana Pembangunan Jangka Menengah Daerah (RPJMD).
(4) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2), diatur lebih lanjut dengan Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 7

(1) To implement the provisions as referred to in Article 6 letter a, the Regional Government carries out victim protection efforts, in the form of:

a. formulating policies on the protection of Children and Women from all forms of acts of violence and discrimination;
b. preparing program and activity planning;
c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure;
d. allocating special gender-responsive budgets; e. establishing PPT and/or Safe Houses;
f. establishing and facilitating FPKK; and
g. conducting monitoring and evaluation.
(2) In the implementation of Regional Government obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government prepares a Regional Action Plan as a basis for SKPD in implementing protection for victims.
(3) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), is part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).
(4) Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), are further regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 8

Pemerintah Daerah menyelenggarakan layanan bagi korban dalam bentuk: a. memfasilitasi pembentukan PPT;

b. memfasilitasi sarana dan prasarana PPT sesuai kemampuan; dan c. memfasilitasi FPKK sebagai wadah jejaring penanganan korban.

translated_text:
Article 8

The Regional Government organizes services for victims in the form of: a. facilitating the establishment of PPT;

b. facilitating PPT facilities and infrastructure according to capacity; and c. facilitating FPKK as a forum for victim handling network.

text:
Pasal 14

(1) Struktur organisasi PPT yang dibentuk oleh Bupati sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 12 ayat (1) terdiri dari:

a. Ketua atau sebutan lain yang setingkat;
b. Sekretaris;
c. Bendahara; dan
d. Ketua Pelaksana yang membawahi bidang-bidang.
(2) Bidang-Bidang sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) huruf d, paling sedikit meliputi:
a. bidang layanan pengaduan;
b. bidang layanan kesehatan;
c. bidang layanan rehabilitasi sosial;
d. bidang pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial;
e. bidang layanan bantuan hukum;
f. bidang kerohanian; dan
g. bidang psikologi

translated_text:
Article 14

(1) The organizational structure of PPT established by the Regent as referred to in Article 12 paragraph (1) consists of:

a. Chairperson or other equivalent designation;
b. Secretary;
c. Treasurer; and
d. Executive Chairperson who oversees the fields.
(2) The Fields as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d, at least include:
a. complaint service field;
b. health service field;
c. social rehabilitation service field;
d. repatriation and social reintegration field;
e. legal aid service field;
f. spiritual field; and
g. psychology field

text:
Pasal 15

Bidang layanan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 14 ayat (2) huruf a memiliki tugas:

a. melakukan wawancara dan observasi keadaan korban;
b. membuat rekomendasi layanan lanjutan;
c. melakukan koordinasi dan rujukan ke layanan lanjutan dan pihak terkait; dan
d. melakukan administrasi proses pengaduan.

translated_text:
Article 15

The complaint service field as referred to in Article 14 paragraph (2) letter a has the tasks of:

a. conducting interviews and observation of the victim's condition;
b. making recommendations for follow-up services;
c. conducting coordination and referral to follow-up services and related parties; and
d. administering the complaint process.

text:
Pasal 16

Bidang layanan kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 14 ayat (2) huruf b memiliki tugas:

a. melakukan pemeriksaan, pengobatan, dan perawatan lanjutan terhadap korban;
b. melakukan koordinasi pelaksanaan rehabilitasi kesehatan dan mediko legal;
c. melakukan pemeriksaan mediko-legal meliputi pengumpulan barang bukti pada korban, pembuatan visum et repertum dan visum et psikiatrikum; d. melakukan pemeriksaan penunjang dan laboratorium terhadap barang bukti;
e. melakukan konsultasi kepada dokter ahli atau melakukan rujukan; dan f. membuat laporan kasus.

translated_text:
Article 16

The health service field as referred to in Article 14 paragraph (2) letter b has the tasks of:

a. conducting examination, treatment, and follow-up care for victims;
b. coordinating the implementation of health rehabilitation and medico-legal;
c. conducting medico-legal examination including collection of evidence from victims, preparation of visum et repertum and visum et psikiatrikum; d. conducting supporting and laboratory examinations of evidence;
e. conducting consultation with specialist doctors or making referrals; and f. making case reports.

text:
Pasal 20

Bidang kerohanian sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 14 ayat (2) huruf f memiliki tugas:

a. melakukan bimbingan rohani kepada korban;
b. melakukan koordinasi dengan pihak terkait; dan
c. membuat laporan dan rekomendasi layanan lanjutan;

translated_text:
Article 20

The field of spiritual guidance as referred to in Article 14 paragraph (2) letter f has the following duties:

a. to provide spiritual guidance to victims;
b. to coordinate with related parties; and
c. to prepare reports and recommendations for follow-up services;

text:
Pasal 22

(1) PPT paling sedikit memiliki 5 (lima ) konselor.

(2) Konselor sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:

a. konselor dalam bidang hukum;
b. konselor dalam bidang kesehatan;
c. konselor dalam bidang psikologi;
d. konselor dalam bidang sosial; dan
e. konselor dalam bidang kerohanian.

translated_text:
Article 22

(1) The PPT must have at least 5 (five) counselors.

(2) Counselors as referred to in paragraph (1) consist of:

a. counselors in the field of law;
b. counselors in the field of health;
c. counselors in the field of psychology;
d. counselors in the field of social affairs; and
e. counselors in the field of spiritual guidance.

text:
Pasal 25

(1) Upaya pencegahan kekerasan terhadap Anak dan Perempuan dilakukan secara terpadu oleh Pemerintah Daerah yang dikoordinasikan oleh instansi yang mempunyai tugas pokok dan fungsi koordinasi di bidang pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.

(2) Upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan dengan cara:

a. membentuk jaringan kerja dalam upaya pencegahan kekerasan dan penanganan tindak kekerasan secara koordinasi, integrasi, sinkronisasi pencegahan kekerasan berdasarkan pola kemitraan;
b. membentuk sistem pencegahan kekerasan, pemetaan lokasi atau wilayah rawan terjadinya tindak kekerasan;
c. menyelenggarakan komunikasi, informasi, dan pendidikan kritis tentang hak-hak anak dan perempuan bagi masyarakat;
d. melakukan sosialisasi tentang peraturan perundang-undangan yang berkaitan dengan perlindungan anak dan perempuan; dan
e. upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan secara terpadu yang dikoordinasi oleh SKPD yang membidangi pemerdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.

translated_text:
Article 25

(1) Efforts to prevent violence against Children and Women shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by the agency having the main duties and coordination functions in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by:

a. establishing a working network for violence prevention efforts and handling acts of violence through coordination, integration, and synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
b. establishing a violence prevention system, mapping locations or areas prone to acts of violence;
c. conducting communication, information, and critical education on the rights of children and women for the community;
d. conducting socialization on laws and regulations related to child and women protection; and
e. prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out in an integrated manner coordinated by the SKPD in charge of women's empowerment and child protection.

text:
Pasal 28

Penyelenggaraan pelayanan terhadap korban dilaksanakan dengan: a. tidak dipungut biaya;

b. cepat;

c. aman dan nyaman;

d. empati;

e. non diskriminasi;

f. terpadu;

g. mudah dijangkau; dan

h. dijamin kerahasiaannya.

translated_text:
Article 28

The provision of services to victims shall be implemented with: a. no charge;

b. speed;

c. safety and comfort;

d. empathy;

e. non-discrimination;

f. integration;

g. easy accessibility; and

h. guaranteed confidentiality.

text:
Pasal 29

Bentuk pelayanan terhadap korban meliputi:

a. pelayanan pengaduan, konsultasi, dan konseling;
b. pelayanan pendampingan;
c. pelayanan kesehatan;
d. pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial;
e. pelayanan hukum;
f. pelayanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial; dan
g. pelayanan psikologi.

translated_text:
Article 29

Forms of services to victims include:

a. complaint, consultation, and counseling services;
b. accompaniment services;
c. health services;
d. social rehabilitation services;
e. legal services;
f. repatriation and social reintegration services; and
g. psychological services.

text:
Pasal 31

Pelayanan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 29 huruf b meliputi:

a. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan dan pemulihan kesehatan;
b. mendampingi korban selama proses medicolegal;
c. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan di Kepolisian, Kejaksaan dan pengadilan;
d. memantau kepentingan dan hak-hak korban dalam proses pemeriksaan di Kepolisan, Kejaksaan dan Pengadilan;
e. menjaga privasi dan kerahasiaan korban dari semua pihak yang tidak berkepentingan, termasuk pemberitaan oleh media massa;
f. melakukan koordinasi dengan pendamping yang lain; dan g. memberikan penanganan yang berkelanjutan hingga tahap rehabilitasi.

translated_text:
Article 31

Accompaniment services as referred to in Article 29 letter b include:

a. accompanying victims during the examination and health recovery process;
b. accompanying victims during the medicolegal process;
c. accompanying victims during the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and court;
d. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
e. protecting the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all unauthorized parties, including reporting by mass media;
f. coordinating with other companions; and g. providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

text:
Pasal 32

Pelayanan kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 29 huruf c meliputi: a. pertolongan pertama kepada korban;

b. perawatan dan pemulihan luka-luka fisik yang bertujuan untuk pemulihan kondisi fisik korban yang dilakukan oleh tenaga medis dan paramedis; dan c. rujukan ke layanan kesehatan.

translated_text:
Article 32

Health services as referred to in Article 29 letter c include: a. first aid to victims;

b. treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of victims carried out by medical and paramedical personnel; and c. referral to health services.

text:
Pasal 40

(1) Dalam upaya menyediakan dan menyelenggarakan penanganan pelayanan dan perlindungan bagi korban, PPT membentuk FPKK.

(2) FPKK sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) bertujuan untuk: a. mengkoordinasikan dan mensinkronisasikan penanganan pelayanan PPT;

b. memelihara dan mengembangkan jejaring serta sistem rujukan; dan c. mengumpulkan, menyusun dan menyajikan laporan kekerasan.

(3) Kepengurusan dan keanggotaan FPKK sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) ditetapkan dengan Keputusan Ketua PTT.

(4) Keanggotaan FPKK sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (3) dikelompokkan dalam peran sebagai berikut:

a. peran kesehatan;
b. peran psikologi;
c. peran hukum;
d. peran sosial; dan
e. peran ekonomi.
(5) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai pembentukan, tugas, pokok, dan fungsi serta keanggotaan FPKK sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diatur lebih lanjut dengan Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 40

(1) In an effort to provide and administer handling of services and protection for victims, PPT establishes FPKK.

(2) FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) aims to: a. coordinate and synchronize the handling of PPT services;

b. maintain and develop networks and referral systems; and c. collect, compile and present reports on violence.

(3) The management and membership of FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) is determined by the Decision of the Chair of PTT.

(4) The membership of FPKK as referred to in paragraph (3) is grouped into the following roles:

a. health role;
b. psychology role;
c. legal role;
d. social role; and
e. economic role.
(5) Further provisions regarding the establishment, main duties, and functions as well as membership of FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) are further regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 41

(1) Dalam rangka mencapai tujuan perlindungan anak dan perempuan dari tindak kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 3, Pemerintah Daerah bekerjasama dengan:

a. Pemerintah;
b. Pemerintah Provinsi;
c. Kabupaten/Kota lain; dan
d. lembaga non Pemerintah.
(2) Kerja sama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi: a. pertukaran data dan informasi;
b. rehabilitasi korban tindak kekerasan;
c. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial; dan
d. penyediaan barang bukti dan saksi, serta ditindaklanjuti sesuai dengan hukum yang berlaku.
(3) Kerjasama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dan ayat (2) dituangkan dalam bentuk Kesepakatan Bersama.

translated_text:
Article 41

(1) In order to achieve the objectives of protecting children and women from acts of violence as referred to in Article 3, the Regional Government cooperates with:

a. the Government;
b. the Provincial Government;
c. other Regencies/Cities; and
d. non-Government institutions.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration; and
d. provision of evidence and witnesses, and followed up in accordance with applicable law.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) is set forth in the form of a Joint Agreement.
